<article class="env-remark" id="68102B">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/68102B">Remark <span data-tag="68102B">7.2.2.3</span>.</a> Let $\calX $ be an $\infty $-topos and $n \geq 0$ an integer. Then the full subcategory of $\Fun (\Delta ^1,\calX )$ consisting of Eilenberg-MacLane objects $p: 1 \rightarrow X$ is stable under finite products. This is clear, since: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(1)$"><p>
A finite product of $n$-connective objects of $\calX $ is $n$-connective (Corollary <a href="/tag/112AFB" data-tag="112AFB">6.5.1.13</a>). 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(2)$"><p>
<em>Any</em> limit of $n$-truncated objects of $\calX $ is $n$-truncated (since $\tau _{\leq n} \calX $ is a localization of $\calX $). 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
</article>